  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings.rs`: The tool page in Properties now owns `tool_page_scroll`. It keeps `Apply` or `Add tool` beside `Close` in a fixed bottom footer.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs`: `tool_shape_editor_window` reserves footer height and displays `ErrorScope::Tool` messages above `Close`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings_grid.rs`: `Tool number` drops `(0 = next free)` from its label and puts that hint in `prop_row_hint`. `Material group`, `Holder diameter`, and `Holder length` gain hover hints.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_body_page.rs` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_body_lathe_page.rs`: Body tab state lines replace `body:`, `draft:`, `placed:`, `placement:`, and `judged` with plain sentences (`In use:`, `Ready to apply:`, `Placed from`, `Placed:`, `Placement error:`). `Tool axis`, `Tip offset`, and `Body frame` use label-left `prop_row` or `prop_row_hint` rows.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_holder_picker.rs` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_profile_page.rs`: `Library holder`, `Gauge length`, and `Projection` align label-left with `num_row` fields. `editor` calls `state.sync_tool_profile_ui()` before it draws the picker.\n- `docs/decisions/2007-tool-editor-footer-plain-state.md`: Records the design choices and the dropped scope.\n\n## Cause\n\nEarlier #2007 changes moved tool settings to Properties and moved shape controls into `Tool shape`, but two items remained open:\n\n1. `tool_settings::page` ran inside the shared scroll area, so `Apply` and `Add tool` scrolled out of view on short viewports while `Close` stayed pinned below.\n2. `Tool number`, the shape-window holder rows, the Body tab placement fields, and Body state lines still used raw labels or jargon. `tool_shape_editor_window` also did not display `ErrorScope::Tool` messages.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all four pass after the final edit):\n\n- `egui_app::tests::structural::tool_properties::tool_page_keeps_apply_and_add_tool_beside_close_without_scrolling`: failed on unchanged `upstream/main` and passed after the fix.\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_body::body_tab_uses_plain_english_state_lines_and_label_left_fields`: failed on unchanged `upstream/main` and passed after the fix.\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_holder_reference::holder_picker_uses_label_left_rows`: failed on unchanged `upstream/main` and passed after the fix.\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_holder::a_shank_the_holder_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name`: updated to check the `Tool shape` window refusal and `Close` containment; failed on `upstream/main` `pages.rs` and passed after the fix.\n\nMutation checks (reverted modified code to `upstream/main`, confirmed FAIL, then restored):\n\n- Revert `pages.rs`, `tool_settings.rs`, and `tool_settings_grid.rs`: `tool_page_keeps_apply_and_add_tool_beside_close_without_scrolling` failed.\n- Revert `tool_body_page.rs`: `body_tab_uses_plain_english_state_lines_and_label_left_fields` failed.\n- Revert `tool_holder_picker.rs` and `tool_profile_page.rs`: `holder_picker_uses_label_left_rows` failed.\n- Revert `pages.rs`: `a_shank_the_holder_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name` failed.\n\nGate and lint after the final edit:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed all 9 steps (0 failed; `ui suites: lib` passed 1283 tests with 7 ignored, plus all 7 mapped integration suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with 0 warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- none (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Full release-lane checks (`gate release`) and ignored snapshot tests (`tool_editor_snapshot` among the 7 ignored tests) did not run.\n- Earlier `gate quick` runs before the clean final pass hit one transient failure in `model_incomplete::incomplete_model_page_and_import_status_name_the_hole_and_post_refusal` (which passed alone in 1 s and passed in the final run) and one `SIGSEGV` in `ui suites: lib` (which passed in the final run).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #2554 (`post_offer_banner`) and PR #2821 (`model_page`) change `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs` in different functions; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n## Review fixes\n\nThe existing-tool heading and actions now require a nonempty Properties target.\nA new-tool draft can match a saved name without opening or deleting an empty tool name.\n\nPin: `egui_app::tests::tool_shape_window::new_tool_matching_saved_name_has_no_empty_target_actions`.\nThe test checks the draft heading, Delete action count, shape action, Apply, and Close.\n\nReview-fix mutation: reverting only the nonempty-name guard failed at the New tool heading assertion. Restoring the guard passed the test (1 passed, 0 failed).\nReview-fix checks:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: all 9 selected steps passed after one failed-step rerun.\n- The first UI lib run exited with `SIGSEGV`. The same step passed on rerun: 1284 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored.\n- All 7 selected integration suites and the UI build passed on the first run.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with 0 warnings.\n\nThe temporary screenshot collector was removed before the gate. No screenshot or review evidence is in the PR branch.\n\n## Before and after screenshots\n\nBoth captures use the same seeded tool and 1280 × 720 shell.\nBefore uses parent `5fdbed9bd8e7a8bb28e6f162a02ab423842b77e8`.\nAfter uses this PR with the review fix.\nThe screenshots are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n| View | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Properties tool page | ![Properties before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/9e0e6ec5f9b1561c4ed14313c72cf18cf11c6911/2875/properties-before.png) | ![Properties after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/9e0e6ec5f9b1561c4ed14313c72cf18cf11c6911/2875/properties-after.png) |\n| Tool shape window | ![Tool shape before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/9e0e6ec5f9b1561c4ed14313c72cf18cf11c6911/2875/tool-shape-before.png) | ![Tool shape after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/9e0e6ec5f9b1561c4ed14313c72cf18cf11c6911/2875/tool-shape-after.png) |\n\nThe Properties images show whether Apply stays beside Close without scrolling.\nThe shape images show the same holder refusal and the aligned library fields.\n\nChangelog: Keep tool Apply and Add beside Close and use plain-English state lines in the tool shape editor.\n\nFixes #2007\n\n",
